<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 August, from 70 to 1999.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/titus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/titus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">70 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,956 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Titus's legions destroy the Second Temple in Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a>, Roman legions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus">Titus</a> retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and destroyed much of the city and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a>. The day, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisha-bav">Tisha B'Av</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> calendar, fell on either 4 or 30 August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus">Titus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1060">1060 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">966 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mirdasids defeat the Fatimids at al-Funaydiq and take Aleppo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mirdasid chieftain Mahmud ibn Nasr of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kilab">Banu Kilab</a> defeated the Fatimid army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-al-dawla">Nasir al-Dawla</a> Ibn Hamdan after its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> allies switched sides. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> then surrendered to Mahmud, ending direct Fatimid rule over the city for good.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1282">1282 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">744 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter III of Aragon lands at Trapani to claim Sicily</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the invitation of the Sicilian rebels of the Vespers, who regarded his wife Constance as their rightful queen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon">Peter III of Aragon</a> landed at Trapani. He was proclaimed king in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> on 4 September, beginning the long Aragonese rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon">Peter III of Aragon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1363">1363 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">663 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Lake Poyang begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fleets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a> clashed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-poyang">Lake Poyang</a> in one of the largest naval battles in history. Zhu's victory weeks later opened his path to founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1464">1464 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">562 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pietro Barbo is elected pope as Paul II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-ii">Pietro Barbo</a>, a Venetian and nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv">Pope Eugene IV</a>, succeeded Pius II as pope, taking the name Paul II. He built the Palazzo Venezia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and amassed a great collection of art and antiquities.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-ii">Pope Paul II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ii">Pope Pius II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Pascoe Fawkner's settlers land at the site of Melbourne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Settlers sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-pascoe-fawkner">John Pascoe Fawkner</a> went ashore on the Yarra River, building the first houses of what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a>. It grew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s second-largest city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ty Cobb makes his major league debut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eighteen-year-old Ty Cobb hit a double in his first game for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a> Tigers. His lifetime batting average of .366 remains the highest in major league history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Washington-Moscow hotline goes into service</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A direct teleprinter link between the White House and the Kremlin began operating. Set up after the Cuban missile crisis, it aimed to prevent war by misunderstanding; it was never a red <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telephone">telephone</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1999">1999 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">27 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Timor votes for independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a UN-run referendum, 78.5 per cent of East Timorese voted for independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Militia violence followed until an Australian-led force restored order; independence came in 2002.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 August <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter of Castile</span><span class="tp">1334–1369</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emily-ruete"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emily-ruete.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emily Ruete</span><span class="tp">1844–1924</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 August <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theodoric-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theodoric the Great</span><span class="tp">454–526</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-alexander-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Alexander III</span><span class="tp">c. 1100–1181</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-xi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis XI</span><span class="tp">1423–1483</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emmanuel-philibert-duke-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emmanuel-philibert-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emmanuel Philibert, Duke of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1528–1580</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihiro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/shimazu-yoshihiro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Shimazu Yoshihiro</span><span class="tp">1535–1619</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-gorbachev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mikhail Gorbachev</span><span class="tp">1931–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
